    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d976">

                <pb facs="0957" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 714.1515/45a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Ewing
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-22T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 22, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inquire whether pending a definite arbitral boundary decision the Government of
                    Honduras would be prepared to withdraw all her troops to the south and east of
                    the Merendén mountains on condition that the Government of Guatemala would
                    likewise withdraw all her troops to the north and west of the Motagua River. The
                    zone lying between these boundaries to be regarded by both Republics as neutral
                    and neither Government to have armed forces therein.</p>
                <p>Report by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
